@Alessio71 You were absolutely right — `-batch` is a **plink.exe** (command-line) option, NOT a **putty.exe** (GUI) option. Our previous "fix" only skipped unknown tools but still passed `-batch` to recognized PuTTY variants, which don't support it either.

**Fixed now** — we've completely removed the `-batch` flag from PuTTY GUI arguments. The `-pw`/`-pwfile` flags handle password passing correctly without `-batch`.

The fix will be in the next nightly build. Thanks for the excellent debugging ...
